-- title:
--   Unipotent, connected or ordinary trichotomy at p for finite flat ρ̄
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a finite field of characteristic $p$, with $p$ an odd prime, and fix a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra structure on $\mathbb{F}_p=\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose structure map has kernel the ideal generated by $p$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, i.e. a $k$-vector space $V$ with $\dim_k V = 2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ that is trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume `IsLocallyFlatCocycleAd` holds for $\bar\rho$, $p$ and the zero cocycle in $Z^1$ of the restriction to $G_p=\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p)$ of the adjoint representation: there is a commutative ring $H$ with a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-Hopf algebra structure, finite and flat as a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module and cocommutative, and a bijection $e$ from the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra maps $H \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ (with their convolution monoid structure) onto $V \times V$ carrying convolution to addition, such that whenever $g = \sigma \circ f$ for $\sigma \in G_p$ one has $e(g) = (\rho(\sigma) (e f)_1, \rho(\sigma) (e f)_2)$, the diagonal action obtained from the zero cocycle. The conclusion is a trichotomy. Either (U) such a Hopf algebra $H$ and equivariant bijection $e$ exist with the Cartier dual over $\mathbb{F}_p$ of $\mathbb{F}_p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} H$ a local ring; or (C) they exist with $\mathbb{F}_p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} H$ itself a local ring; or (O) there is a $k$-subspace $V_1 \subseteq V$ of dimension $1$, stable under $\rho(\sigma)$ for all $\sigma \in G_p$ (pushed to the global Galois group by `primeLocalToGlobal`), with $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in V_1$ for every $v \in V$ and every $\sigma$ lying in the inertia subgroup of the valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ over $\mathbb{Q}_p$, and such that for any such inertial $\sigma$ and any natural number $c$ with $\sigma\zeta = \zeta^c$ for all $\zeta$ with $\zeta^p=1$, $\rho(\sigma)$ acts on $V_1$ as multiplication by the image of $c$ in $k$.
--
--   This is the local classification, at the prime $p$, of a two-dimensional mod $p$ representation whose restriction to $G_p$ admits a finite flat model: the model has unipotent special fibre, or connected special fibre, or the representation is ordinary with the inertial action on the stable line given by the mod $p$ cyclotomic character. It feeds the finiteness and dimension bound for the local flat deformation classes at $p$ via [`ResidualGaloisRep.finiteDimensional_localFlatClassesAd_and_finrank_le`](thm.html#ResidualGaloisRep.finiteDimensional_localFlatClassesAd_and_finrank_le).
